    <GaugingStation location="Burnham Overy" name="Burn" number="34012">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Crump weir gauging a gw influenced, rural catchment with Chalk bedrock overlain with superficial deposits and with only minor artificial influences, station is bypassed at high flows.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Bypasses at 2.3 cumecs. Can be affected by mill operations c 50m u/s. One rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Compound Crump weir with three sections - central low flow crest 0.6m, flanked by two crests 1.2m wide each.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Low flows in summer 2005 and 2008 affected by u/s mill operation. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Gw-influenced regime, annual hydrographs reflect high baseflow component from the Chalk aquifer. Industrial/agricultural abstraction reduces natural runoff but impacts are minimal. Effluent returns increase runoff and may produce a minor net import from outside the catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Predominantly Boulder Clay with some sand and gravel, underlying Chalk exposed in the valleys. Rural, predominantly arable.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">GEI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED. Good fit to rating." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="AMAX3 is contained and flow is modular." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
